            "parents": [
                "20d2e853c25fbc0ae4d566f99a4b0834c9e21676"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/15/90515/2",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Angela Cheng wiwynn",
                "email": "angelaptcheng@gmail.com",
                "username": "AngelaPTCheng"
            },
            "createdOn": 1779780051,
            "author": {
                "name": "Angela Cheng wiwynn",
                "email": "angelaptcheng@gmail.com",
                "username": "AngelaPTCheng"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "common/src/software_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 204,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Agree that there needs to be some kind of mechanism to prevent concurrent initialization of the same configuration.\n\nI did not hit that issue in my testing since usually EM was already running when i tested, so there was usually only the mapper result or the match (EM restart/changes) causing this handler to be called.\n\nnitpick: since we run the same logic on every return path, we can use a wrapper function to only write it once and keep the initialization state tracking logic contained there.\n\n```suggestion\nsdbusplus::async::task<void> SoftwareManager::handleInterfaceAdded(\n    const std::string& service, const std::string& path,\n    const std::string& interface)\n{\n    if (devices.contains(path) || initializingPaths.contains(path))\n    {\n        debug(\"Skipping duplicate init for {PATH}\", \"PATH\", path);\n        co_return;\n    }\n\n    initializingPaths.insert(path);\n    co_await handleInterfaceAddedGuarded(service, path, interface);\n    initializingPaths.erase(path);\n}\n\nsdbusplus::async::task<void> SoftwareManager::handleInterfaceAddedGuarded(\n    const std::string& service, const std::string& path,\n    const std::string& interface)\n{\n   // ... same as before, besides the renaming\n}\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/src/software_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 204,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Angela Cheng wiwynn",
                        "email": "angelaptcheng@gmail.com",
                        "username": "AngelaPTCheng"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nI refactored handleInterfaceAdded() into a wrapper and moved the original\ninitialization flow into handleInterfaceAddedGuarded(). This keeps the\ninitializingPaths tracking logic in one place.\n\nPlease take another look when you have a chance."
                }
            ],
